2026-06-29 11:24:24,561 | AGENT | AIInnovation Agent received: The client expects an artificial intelligence solution capable of facilitating access to information, improving quality of answers, reducing times of processing, and providing a high level of relevance of the answers. How can we design the AI components and innovation strategy for this tender response to meet these requirements?
2026-06-29 11:26:03,484 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-06-29 11:26:03,484 | AGENT | AIInnovation Agent answered: To address the client's expectations, our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l., can leverage its expertise in AI research and development, particularly in large language models (LLMs) and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) capabilities. 

We propose designing an AI solution centered around our preferred sovereign model, Mistral 7B Instruct, which offers strong French-language performance and is self-hostable, aligning with the client's potential need for data sovereignty. This model can be fine-tuned using our established methods such as LoRA, QLoRA, or full fine-tuning on a domain-specific corpus to improve its accuracy in providing relevant answers within the context of administrative services.

To facilitate access to information and improve the quality of answers, we will implement a RAG system. This involves integrating a robust retrieval strategy, such as dense vector (semantic) search or BM25 sparse search, with our Mistral 7B Instruct model. The RAG approach allows for more accurate and context-specific responses by retrieving relevant information from internal procedures, applicable regulatory texts, and other documents before generating an answer.

Our innovation strategy will focus on continuous improvement through quarterly fine-tuning of the model on anonymized data, ensuring compliance with GDPR regulations. We will also prioritize explicability and transparency in our solution, incorporating methods like source citation (RAG grounding), chain-of-thought display, SHAP for classification models, and LIME to provide clear explanations for the recommendations or proposals made by the AI system.

To reduce processing times while maintaining a high level of relevance, we can utilize quantization methods such as INT8 or GPTQ to optimize the model's performance without significantly compromising its accuracy. Our goal is to achieve response times compatible with daily use by agents, aiming for a time of response under 2 seconds for current requests.

In terms of integration, our solution will be designed to work seamlessly with existing practices and systems, including business software, civil status, town planning, electronic management of documents (EDM), and user directories. We recognize the importance of sovereignty and data protection, ensuring that all data is hosted within the European Union and protected appropriately through encryption and anonymization if necessary.

Our approach will also include a progressive deployment strategy, starting with a pilot phase on a limited scope before generalizing to all services. This phased rollout will be accompanied by comprehensive training for agents to ensure a smooth transition and optimal use of the AI solution.

By leveraging our strengths in AI research and development, particularly in LLMs and RAG capabilities, along with a focus on innovation, explicability, and compliance with regulatory requirements, we believe Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can deliver an artificial intelligence solution that meets the client's expectations for improving access to information, answer quality, processing times, and relevance.
